{"title":"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1c","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1\">Problem 1</a></span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=T-1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Three schools each sent four students to a competition. The scores earned by nine of the students are given in the table below. The scores of the remaining three students are represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/5/32581661cddf01ad30c1e36efe72f99eb0a0adca.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x, y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"27\" height=\"11\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />. The total score for any school is determined by adding the scores of the four students competing from the school.----\n<i>An image is supposed to go here.  You can help us out by creating one and <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit\">editing it in</a></span>.  Thanks.</i>\n</p>\n<hr />\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The total scores for Schools A and B are the same. What is the value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />, the score for Student 4 at School B?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1c&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>From <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1a\" title=\"2016 CEMC Fryer Problems/Problem 1a\">part a</a>, the total score for School A was <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/e/5/ce5d3cbb9ab0a992ed503c2d4499e4f4af2f9d65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Since the score for Student 4 at School C is twice the score for Student 3 at the same school, we know <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/c/b/0cbbf3f5379d42ef80b3bd0a4d67dce24ace6a3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z = 2y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"51\" height=\"15\" />. The total score for School C is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/4/3/7436b8d54c11531ac8704668170f49eb704fbbb1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9 + 15 + y + 2y = 3y + 24$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"207\" height=\"17\" />.\n</p><p>This must be equal to the total score at school A, so we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/4/fd46506239a95f61f77010abf2231ac6935fd233.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y + 24 = 36$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"103\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/9/b795373ff6387aa823b82d2a0da6140cc2ea9362.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3y = 36 - 24 = 12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"146\" height=\"17\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/9/5/f957a62eab89fd12c4048f21cbf318d322c11e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y = \\frac{12}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"58\" height=\"38\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/e/2/8e26ab041cffa4c51682e683f352d0122143e999.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{y = 4}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"56\" height=\"29\" />, the score for Student 3 at School C\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/3/b13f21416d84e13708696f34dea81026cda583c9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />, the score for Student 4 at School C, is then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/1/251347a53914f100e471f1ccf3d62c127463cae8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\times 4 = \\boxed{8}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"87\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018002002\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.023 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 54/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 1139/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 5/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 2165/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.159      1 2016_CEMC_Fryer_Problems/Problem_1\n100.00%   13.159      1 -total\n 40.47%    5.325      1 Template:Image_needed\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:36954:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018002002 and revision id 285810. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}